{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline skills are fine for a demo, but real skills live somewhere: a folder in\nyour repo, a bundle baked at build time, or rows in a database. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SkillSource"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis how "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" reads them. This page covers the three built-in sources and\nhow to combine them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every source is bytes only, so the same middleware works on the edge, in a\nWorker, or on a server. Pick the source that matches where your skills live."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"from-a-folder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From a folder"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillDirectory"},{"type":"text","value":" walks a folder for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" files. It lives under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/node"},{"type":"text","value":"\nentry point because it reads the filesystem, so use it on a server, not the edge."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { skillDirectory } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skillDirectory('./skills'))],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A skill folder is any directory that contains a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":". Bundled files under\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"references/"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assets/"},{"type":"text","value":" become the skill's resources, and files under\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/"},{"type":"text","value":" are listed too (they are inventoried, not run, in this release)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillDirectory"},{"type":"text","value":" is strict: a malformed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" is an error, so a\nbroken file never slips into your catalog silently. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ strict: false }"},{"type":"text","value":" to\nskip bad files and load the rest."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"from-a-build-time-bundle-edge-safe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From a build-time bundle (edge-safe)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an edge deployment you cannot read the filesystem at request time. The Vite\nplugin globs your skills at build time and bakes them into the bundle, so\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staticSkills"},{"type":"text","value":" needs no filesystem at runtime."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the plugin to your Vite config:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { skillsCatalogPlugin } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [skillsCatalogPlugin({ dir: 'skills' })],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then wrap the generated catalog:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { staticSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/static'\nimport { catalog } from 'virtual:tanstack-skills'\n\nconst skills = staticSkills(catalog)\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skills)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because the catalog is baked at build time, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills.names"},{"type":"text","value":" is a typed list of\nyour skill names, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" tool's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" is constrained to it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"from-your-own-store","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From your own store"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For DB, S3, or registry-backed skills, define a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SkillSource"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself. It is a\nsmall interface: list the skills, and load one by name. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./writing-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a skill source"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full walkthrough and the\nconformance suite that proves your adapter behaves."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"combine-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine sources"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Real setups layer skills: org-wide, per-project, per-tenant. Combine them with\nthe combinators, then pass the result to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { aggregate, dedupe } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\n// Org skills plus this tenant's skills, org first on a name clash.\nconst source = dedupe(aggregate([orgSkills, tenantSkills]))","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combinator"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregate([a, b])"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concatenate sources in order. No dedupe."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dedupe(source)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First occurrence of a name wins, warns on a clash."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter(source, fn)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hide skills your predicate rejects. Hidden skills never reach the catalog."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cache(source)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memoize "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"list()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load()"},{"type":"text","value":". Shares one fetch across concurrent calls."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing an array straight to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills([a, b])"},{"type":"text","value":" is shorthand for\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dedupe(aggregate([a, b]))"},{"type":"text","value":". A single source is used as-is and never wrapped, so\na tenant-scoped source is never cached into a shared bucket by accident. Reach\nfor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cache"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself only when the source is safe to share."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable Agent Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the middleware, the catalog, and the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":" flow."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./writing-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a skill source"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — back skills with your own store."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"from-a-folder","text":"From a folder","level":2},{"id":"from-a-build-time-bundle-edge-safe","text":"From a build-time bundle (edge-safe)","level":2},{"id":"from-your-own-store","text":"From your own store","level":2},{"id":"combine-sources","text":"Combine sources","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInline skills are fine for a demo, but real skills live somewhere: a folder in\nyour repo, a bundle baked at build time, or rows in a database. A `SkillSource`\nis how `withSkills` reads them. This page covers the three built-in sources and\nhow to combine them.\n\nEvery source is bytes only, so the same middleware works on the edge, in a\nWorker, or on a server. Pick the source that matches where your skills live.\n\n## From a folder\n\n`skillDirectory` walks a folder for `SKILL.md` files. It lives under the `/node`\nentry point because it reads the filesystem, so use it on a server, not the edge.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { skillDirectory } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skillDirectory('./skills'))],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nA skill folder is any directory that contains a `SKILL.md`. Bundled files under\n`references/` and `assets/` become the skill's resources, and files under\n`scripts/` are listed too (they are inventoried, not run, in this release).\n\nBy default `skillDirectory` is strict: a malformed `SKILL.md` is an error, so a\nbroken file never slips into your catalog silently. Pass `{ strict: false }` to\nskip bad files and load the rest.\n\n## From a build-time bundle (edge-safe)\n\nFor an edge deployment you cannot read the filesystem at request time. The Vite\nplugin globs your skills at build time and bakes them into the bundle, so\n`staticSkills` needs no filesystem at runtime.\n\nAdd the plugin to your Vite config:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { skillsCatalogPlugin } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [skillsCatalogPlugin({ dir: 'skills' })],\n})\n```\n\nThen wrap the generated catalog:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { staticSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/static'\nimport { catalog } from 'virtual:tanstack-skills'\n\nconst skills = staticSkills(catalog)\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skills)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nBecause the catalog is baked at build time, `skills.names` is a typed list of\nyour skill names, and the `load_skill` tool's `name` is constrained to it.\n\n## From your own store\n\nFor DB, S3, or registry-backed skills, define a `SkillSource` yourself. It is a\nsmall interface: list the skills, and load one by name. See\n[Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) for the full walkthrough and the\nconformance suite that proves your adapter behaves.\n\n## Combine sources\n\nReal setups layer skills: org-wide, per-project, per-tenant. Combine them with\nthe combinators, then pass the result to `withSkills`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { aggregate, dedupe } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\n// Org skills plus this tenant's skills, org first on a name clash.\nconst source = dedupe(aggregate([orgSkills, tenantSkills]))\n```\n\n| Combinator | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `aggregate([a, b])` | Concatenate sources in order. No dedupe. |\n| `dedupe(source)` | First occurrence of a name wins, warns on a clash. |\n| `filter(source, fn)` | Hide skills your predicate rejects. Hidden skills never reach the catalog. |\n| `cache(source)` | Memoize `list()` and `load()`. Shares one fetch across concurrent calls. |\n\nPassing an array straight to `withSkills([a, b])` is shorthand for\n`dedupe(aggregate([a, b]))`. A single source is used as-is and never wrapped, so\na tenant-scoped source is never cached into a shared bucket by accident. Reach\nfor `cache` yourself only when the source is safe to share.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Portable Agent Skills](./agent-skills) — the middleware, the catalog, and the\n  `load_skill` flow.\n- [Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) — back skills with your own store.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Skill Sources\nid: skill-sources\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Load portable Agent Skills from a folder, a build-time bundle, or your own store, and combine several sources with aggregate, dedupe, filter, and cache.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - skill sources\n  - skillDirectory\n  - staticSkills\n  - inlineSkill\n  - skill catalog\n  - edge skills\n---\n\nInline skills are fine for a demo, but real skills live somewhere: a folder in\nyour repo, a bundle baked at build time, or rows in a database. A `SkillSource`\nis how `withSkills` reads them. This page covers the three built-in sources and\nhow to combine them.\n\nEvery source is bytes only, so the same middleware works on the edge, in a\nWorker, or on a server. Pick the source that matches where your skills live.\n\n## From a folder\n\n`skillDirectory` walks a folder for `SKILL.md` files. It lives under the `/node`\nentry point because it reads the filesystem, so use it on a server, not the edge.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { skillDirectory } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skillDirectory('./skills'))],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nA skill folder is any directory that contains a `SKILL.md`. Bundled files under\n`references/` and `assets/` become the skill's resources, and files under\n`scripts/` are listed too (they are inventoried, not run, in this release).\n\nBy default `skillDirectory` is strict: a malformed `SKILL.md` is an error, so a\nbroken file never slips into your catalog silently. Pass `{ strict: false }` to\nskip bad files and load the rest.\n\n## From a build-time bundle (edge-safe)\n\nFor an edge deployment you cannot read the filesystem at request time. The Vite\nplugin globs your skills at build time and bakes them into the bundle, so\n`staticSkills` needs no filesystem at runtime.\n\nAdd the plugin to your Vite config:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { skillsCatalogPlugin } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/node'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [skillsCatalogPlugin({ dir: 'skills' })],\n})\n```\n\nThen wrap the generated catalog:\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { withSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\nimport { staticSkills } from '@tanstack/ai-skills/static'\nimport { catalog } from 'virtual:tanstack-skills'\n\nconst skills = staticSkills(catalog)\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withSkills(skills)],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nBecause the catalog is baked at build time, `skills.names` is a typed list of\nyour skill names, and the `load_skill` tool's `name` is constrained to it.\n\n## From your own store\n\nFor DB, S3, or registry-backed skills, define a `SkillSource` yourself. It is a\nsmall interface: list the skills, and load one by name. See\n[Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) for the full walkthrough and the\nconformance suite that proves your adapter behaves.\n\n## Combine sources\n\nReal setups layer skills: org-wide, per-project, per-tenant. Combine them with\nthe combinators, then pass the result to `withSkills`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { aggregate, dedupe } from '@tanstack/ai-skills'\n\n// Org skills plus this tenant's skills, org first on a name clash.\nconst source = dedupe(aggregate([orgSkills, tenantSkills]))\n```\n\n| Combinator | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `aggregate([a, b])` | Concatenate sources in order. No dedupe. |\n| `dedupe(source)` | First occurrence of a name wins, warns on a clash. |\n| `filter(source, fn)` | Hide skills your predicate rejects. Hidden skills never reach the catalog. |\n| `cache(source)` | Memoize `list()` and `load()`. Shares one fetch across concurrent calls. |\n\nPassing an array straight to `withSkills([a, b])` is shorthand for\n`dedupe(aggregate([a, b]))`. A single source is used as-is and never wrapped, so\na tenant-scoped source is never cached into a shared bucket by accident. Reach\nfor `cache` yourself only when the source is safe to share.\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Portable Agent Skills](./agent-skills) — the middleware, the catalog, and the\n  `load_skill` flow.\n- [Write a skill source](./writing-adapters) — back skills with your own store.\n"}
